{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30153 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Lucidenate Q appears to exert its biological effect through a complex pathway involving the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including Methyl Lucidenate Q, and is itself a target of several metabolic intermediates such as Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and a structurally complex molecule. The final link in this chain is the CD276 antigen, which is targeted by all these intermediates. This suggests that Methyl Lucidenate Q may act as a modulator of a metabolic pathway that ultimately leads to the activation or targeting of CD276 antigen. The evidence implies a potential role for Methyl Lucidenate Q in influencing the expression or activity of CD276 antigen through a series of enzymatic and metabolic interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
